      "rendered_text": "<div class='absent'><strong>Randomised-contrast disclosure (per pooled trial, from the registry arm structure &mdash; disclosed, not an adjustment).</strong> Eligibility should test what actually DIFFERS between the randomised arms, not the mere presence of the drug word: a trial giving the drug of interest as BACKGROUND in every arm (e.g. all arms on the same agent, randomising a different drug) is not a randomised comparison of it. For each pooled trial the randomised contrast is reconstructed from AACT <code>design_groups</code> + <code>interventions</code>: <strong>3 of 3</strong> pooled trials have a registry-confirmed contrast (the intervention of interest differs across arms). A trial with no registry arm data, or coded under a class label / development code we cannot machine-match, is shown as <em>contrast unverified</em> &mdash; a VISIBLE fail-open state, never silently treated as verified. <table class='arms'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Contrast status</th><th>Randomised difference</th></tr><tr><td>30990260</td><td>randomised contrast verified</td><td title='the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms (registry-confirmed contrast)'>canagliflozin</td></tr><tr><td>32970396</td><td>randomised contrast verified</td><td title='the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms (registry-confirmed contrast)'>dapagliflozin</td></tr><tr><td>36331190</td><td>randomised contrast verified</td><td title='the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms (registry-confirmed contrast)'>empagliflozin</td></tr></table></div>",
